research/audit/wave5-dispatch/audit-alpha-a8-round3.result.json:16:  "tail": "A8 round 3 is complete. Both jobs done.\n\n## 1. Five items, six rows adjudicated — 108 total, none outstanding\n\n| item | lane(s) | outcome |\n|---|---|---|\n| `cex-unbounded-with-convergent-subsequence` | **both** | **confirmed_fatal** (`dependency_citation`) |\n| `def-interval` | deepseek | false_positive |\n| `cex-cauchy-rationals-no-rational-limit` | deepseek | false_positive |\n| `cor-monotone-converges-iff-bounded` | deepseek | confirmed_nonfatal |\n| `lem-geometric-sequence-null` | deepseek | confirmed_nonfatal |\n\n**I touched exactly one item: `cex-unbounded-with-convergent-subsequence`.** Its Remark claimed that replacing the unbounded branch with a second constant \"gives\" `ex-two-subsequential-limits`. It does not — that item is $(-1)^k(1+1/k)$, and *its own Remark* says replacing the perturbation by a constant collapses it to the plain alternating sequence. The math asserted was true; the identification was false. Remark-only repair, `impact-audit` 0 interfaces / 0 items, certified independently (Sonnet, CERTIFY, 0 fatal 0 nonfatal), `verification.verified` written, `step8-guard` 1/1 licensed.\n\n**`def-interval` is not self-contradictory.** The item's next paragraph states that $\\pm\\infty$ are notation marking the absence of an endpoint condition. What settles it is the form DeepSeek didn't look at: $(-\\infty,\\infty)$ is listed as *both* open and closed, which is correct ($\\mathbb{R}$ is clopen) and is only coherent under the item's own convention — under DeepSeek's reading it could not be closed at all. No repair, so its 25-edge cone is untouched.\n\n**`cor-monotone-converges-iff-bounded` is converging, not thrashing.** `[L5]` is pre-existing text my round-2 repair never touched; the two findings are disjoint in location and cause, and only one is fatal. Its fact list does not need a unit rewrite — the other four facts were each verified exact by the round-2 certifier. Stopping condition on record: a third distinct **fatal** reopens the Statement; a third nonfatal does not, since nonfatals license no edit at all.\n\nOn `lem-geometric-sequence-null` DeepSeek is half right — step 3.5 genuinely escapes `[L9]` (M may be negative), step 3.6 does not. Both nonfatal.\n\n## 2. Coverage receipt attested\n\nReviewer, attestation, and all three drift reasons written (via a kept script, so it's reproducible). **All three `audit-receipt-*` error classes are gone**; `level-coverage --audit` now reports 3 errors, none receipt-class: the missing spine receipt (yours) and the two confirmed-fatal rows that clear on rejudge.\n\nThe attestation records against interest, as asked: the Sonnet lane refused 207 calls at concurrency 16 and its verdicts exist only via the concurrency-4 replay; coverage is current for **178 items, not 209**; Sonnet is not a cross-family screen; and paired coverage before this round was 205/209, with 4 DeepSeek nulls — all four on the same page my repair re-froze, so one rejudge closes both.\n\n**Rejudge list: the same 31 items** (whole `monotone-sequences-and-cauchy-completeness` A/B pair), recomputed over all 209 contexts, 62 verdicts — command in `wave5-alpha.md` § \"The exact rejudge list\". Second consecutive round where a Remark-only edit changing zero public interfaces invalidated 31 frozen contexts; that's now measured twice and belongs in A10.\n\nStill yours: the rejudge, `wave5-spine-audit.json`, and `RESUME.md` still headed WAVE 4."
