research/audit/wave9-dispatch/audit-refuter-a6r3-thm-baire-one-continuity-points.result.json:16:  "tail": "VERDICT: CLEAN\n\nBOUNDARY: The proof operates entirely on nondegenerate intervals ($a<b$, $c<d$) and constructs strictly nested subintervals. Oscillation at interior points is handled via the monotonicity of $\\omega_f$ and the neighbourhood construction; endpoint and isolated-point cases either are excluded by the domain $[a,b]$ or are harmless. The interval form of Baire category (L5) is correctly applied to nondegenerate $[c,d]$. All boundary checks (empty, zero, one, degenerate, endpoints, nonempty-choice) pass; no boundary flaw was found.\n\nSOURCES: Every cited dependency (def-baire-class-one, def-oscillation, lem-oscillation-superlevel-sets-are-closed, lem-baire-category-in-a-closed-interval, thm-discontinuity-set-is-f-sigma, def-nowhere-dense-meager, def-f-sigma-g-delta, def-open-and-closed-in-r, thm-open-set-algebra-r, thm-continuity-preimage-characterisation, thm-algebra-of-continuous-functions, def-continuity-real, def-interval, cor-archimedean-reciprocal, def-canonical-natural, lem-of-naturals-positive, def-real-limit, def-sequence, lem-of-abs-value, def-max-min, def-neighbourhood-r, def-interior-closure-boundary-r, def-limit-point-r) was inspected. Every fact (L1–L12) quotes its source exactly, and each application in the proof matches the stated theorem or definition.\n\nCHECKED: The title, public claim (all four sub‑claims), every numbered step (1.1 through 11.1), and the Remarks were examined. No logical gap, missing hypothesis, circularity, or citation mismatch was found."
